! **The collinear limit of a noncollinear run, and the only reason it exists.**
! `h-atom-lsda.in`'s cell, atom, cutoff and smearing, with the spin regime
! changed and nothing else: the moment is put along `+z` (`angle1 = 0`), where
! `h10-chain-noncolin.in` puts its moments in the plane.
!
! Without spin-orbit coupling the noncollinear Hamiltonian of a state polarized
! along `z` block-diagonalises into the two collinear ones, so every quantity
! this run produces has to match `h-atom-lsda.in`'s exactly -- including the
! *projected* density of states, whose two spin channels are then the LSDA run's
! two channels. That identity is what validates `partialdos_nc`'s up/down split
! here, where no `projwfc.x` reference for a noncollinear run without spin-orbit
! coupling has been generated.
!
! **Saturated on purpose.** One electron, so `zeta = 1` at every point carrying
! any density -- which is the boundary the exchange-correlation clamp sits on.
! The minority potential there was discontinuous in the last bit of `zeta` until
! 2026-09-12 (`jnp.clip` splits a tangent evenly at a tie, so the boundary got
! half the interior's), and this pair of runs is what found it: the same ground
! state reached two ways lands on opposite sides of it by rounding alone.
!
! `nbnd` is doubled because a spinor band holds one electron.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1, celldm(1) = 12.0,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.02
    noncolin = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
    angle1(1) = 0.0
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 1 0 0 0
